00:13:42.473 --> 00:13:45.737
Piss poor execution?
Hell no.

256
00:13:45.825 --> 00:13:47.827
Look. I don't get
why we patch up people

257
00:13:47.957 --> 00:13:49.959
and then let
them go kill each other.

258
00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:53.963
You pick a side. you treat them.
you have their loyalty forever.

259
00:13:54.094 --> 00:13:55.835
That is the safe play.

260
00:13:57.358 --> 00:14:00.927
Well. the safest play
is to kill 'em all.

261
00:14:03.799 --> 00:14:06.976
Well.
The lady has a good point.

262
00:14:07.107 --> 00:14:10.327
Of course. then
who would plant the fields?

263
00:14:10.458 --> 00:14:12.025
Who would fix the sewers?

264
00:14:12.112 --> 00:14:13.896
Who would protect our homes?

265
00:14:14.549 --> 00:14:17.900
Yes. I can make a choice
that would save us today.

266
00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:19.771
But it might lead
to our deaths a month.

267
00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:21.338
a year. a decade from now.

268
00:14:21.469 --> 00:14:26.039
So I am not making any decision
until I have all the facts.

269
00:14:33.742 --> 00:14:36.092
-My turn!
-Everything is fine.

270
00:14:36.223 --> 00:14:39.052
Okay. it's just
a temporary loss in voltage.

271
00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:40.507
This has happened before.
We'll be okay.

272
00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.230
-He's in a lot of pain.
-I know.

273
00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.753
We're gonna get something
for it.

274
00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.120
Did Damien breathe in any smoke?

275
00:14:46.146 --> 00:14:47.538
We all did.

276
00:14:47.625 --> 00:14:50.585
-Belleville burnt down our home.
-Are you their leader?

277
00:14:50.715 --> 00:14:52.630
Bauer said your people
started the fire.

278
00:14:52.761 --> 00:14:55.111
Of course he did.
He's a liar and a monster.

279
00:14:55.242 --> 00:14:56.678
Luis! He's having trouble
breathing.

280
00:15:00.725 --> 00:15:02.553
It's Ray.
He's not doing so good.

281
00:15:03.293 --> 00:15:05.774
Hershel. sterilize his
neck under his Adam's apple.

282
00:15:10.518 --> 00:15:11.911
This guy's bleeding out fast.

283
00:15:11.998 --> 00:15:13.584
I'm gonna have to get
him stabilized first.

284
00:15:13.608 --> 00:15:15.436
Don't you dare.
Doctor's been treating

285
00:15:15.566 --> 00:15:16.848
your people for the past
two hours.

286
00:15:16.872 --> 00:15:17.873
Mine are dying.

287
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.831
The only person to blame is you.
Claudia.

288
00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.442
They're dying because of you.

289
00:15:26.186 --> 00:15:27.404
Help Damien.

290
00:15:28.231 --> 00:15:29.667
Help him now.

291
00:15:29.754 --> 00:15:32.627
Whether or not you threaten me.
I'm gonna help his people.

292
00:15:32.714 --> 00:15:34.542
And I'm gonna help yours too.

293
00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.087
Anyone who isn't
a hospital worker. a patient.

294
00:15:58.174 --> 00:16:00.655
or a guard needs to leave
this ER immediately.

295
00:16:02.048 --> 00:16:03.048
Let's go!

296
00:16:10.099 --> 00:16:11.598
Hershel. I'm going
to treat this wound

297
00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:13.450
while you do the cricothyrotomy.

298
00:16:14.234 --> 00:16:16.366
-By myself?
-I'll guide you through it.

299
00:16:16.497 --> 00:16:18.325
Look. cutting a throat open
sounds rough.

300
00:16:18.455 --> 00:16:20.695
but it's a lot less complicated
than a compound fracture.

301
00:16:21.937 --> 00:16:23.504
We can save both their lives.

302
00:16:23.634 --> 00:16:25.071
but it means you have
to do this.

303
00:16:26.463 --> 00:16:27.551
Okay.

304
00:16:28.074 --> 00:16:29.834
Ellis. I need you
to take the Belleville people

305
00:16:29.858 --> 00:16:30.902
to the apartments.

306
00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.097
Rose. the Newark people
to the beach.

307
00:16:32.121 --> 00:16:34.254
and I want five extra guards
on each.

308
00:16:34.341 --> 00:16:36.691
And tell the team downstairs
to keep the tanks full.

309
00:16:36.821 --> 00:16:38.364
The power cannot go out.
Do you understand?

310
00:16:38.388 --> 00:16:39.388
Go.

311
00:16:47.745 --> 00:16:52.402
Hey. just the two guards
I've been looking for.

312
00:16:52.489 --> 00:16:54.424
Max down in the armory
is looking for both of you.

313
00:16:54.448 --> 00:16:56.319
I will take these two.

314
00:16:57.451 --> 00:16:59.801
Door over there.
Let's go.

315
00:17:07.329 --> 00:17:11.551
Ray? That's your name. right?
Stay with me. Ray.

316
00:17:11.856 --> 00:17:13.380
Can you tell me what happened?

317
00:17:13.467 --> 00:17:15.425
Newark boy did that.
He put an arrow through

318
00:17:15.512 --> 00:17:17.862
Ray's little girl and then
beat him with a crowbar.

319
00:17:19.777 --> 00:17:21.040
He's here.

320
00:17:22.301 --> 00:17:25.044
Ray. we've got to prevent
infection. stop blood loss.

321
00:17:25.174 --> 00:17:26.393
and stabilize your fracture.

322
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.284
but we can't do that
until we manage your pain.

323
00:17:28.308 --> 00:17:30.179
-You feel me?
-What is it?

324
00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:33.182
I call that the Neil Armstrong.
It's mostly whiskey and Tang.

325
00:17:33.269 --> 00:17:34.618
Alright.
Ready. Ray?

326
00:17:38.492 --> 00:17:39.884
Drink as much as you can.

327
00:17:46.935 --> 00:17:48.937
Hershel? Let's go.

328
00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:51.244
I need you to feel for
the Adam's apple.

329
00:17:51.374 --> 00:17:53.202
Move your fingers just below it.

330
00:17:53.289 --> 00:17:54.899
That's
the cricothyroid membrane.

331
00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.292
-You got it?
-Yeah. I got it.

332
00:17:56.379 --> 00:17:58.512
Make the incision
just above that.

333
00:17:58.599 --> 00:18:01.167
Talk to me. Hershel.
Can you feel the membrane?

334
00:18:01.254 --> 00:18:02.037
-Yeah.
-Good.

335
00:18:02.168 --> 00:18:03.560
Now you got to pierce it.

336
00:18:03.691 --> 00:18:05.345
One breath. one motion.

337
00:18:09.392 --> 00:18:11.090
Okay. Got it.

338
00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:12.613
Now slide the tube in.

339
00:18:18.314 --> 00:18:20.447
Doctor.
we need you over here.

340
00:18:20.534 --> 00:18:21.883
I'll be over there soon.

341
00:18:47.474 --> 00:18:48.474
Ray.

342
00:18:49.737 --> 00:18:51.260
Ray?

343
00:18:51.913 --> 00:18:53.436
Is he all right?

344
00:18:53.523 --> 00:18:55.656
He passed out.
Pulse is good.

345
00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.267
I think Ray's good.

346
00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.269
We're good.

347
00:19:08.059 --> 00:19:09.191
Can you check on bed eight?

348
00:19:09.322 --> 00:19:11.193
I've got three more surgeries
to prep for.

349
00:19:11.324 --> 00:19:12.325
Yeah.

350
00:19:27.035 --> 00:19:28.558
She could have killed
my brother.

351
00:19:28.645 --> 00:19:31.344
-Our only doctor.
-But we didn't let that happen.

352
00:19:31.431 --> 00:19:33.955
Belleville outnumbers us.
So does Newark.

353
00:19:34.042 --> 00:19:35.522
What if...
What if we heal them

354
00:19:35.652 --> 00:19:37.219
only for one of them
to take over?

355
00:19:37.306 --> 00:19:38.655
Completely wipe us out?

356
00:19:38.742 --> 00:19:40.527
I know that I have
to make a choice here.

357
00:19:40.657 --> 00:19:43.138
but what if there is
no right choice?

358
00:19:43.269 --> 00:19:45.116
Anybody who tells you
that the solution's simple

359
00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.273
is answering the wrong question.

360
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.406
Picking one side.
killing the other. that's easy.

361
00:19:51.059 --> 00:19:54.976
Building a safe community is
the hardest thing in the world.

362
00:19:59.023 --> 00:20:01.461
I don't know if there's
a right choice.

363
00:20:02.462 --> 00:20:05.856
But if there is.
you're gonna make it.

364
00:20:09.556 --> 00:20:12.385
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

365
00:20:14.691 --> 00:20:15.910
Do you regret doing it?

366
00:20:17.477 --> 00:20:18.477
No.

367
00:20:19.783 --> 00:20:21.089
Do you?

368
00:20:25.485 --> 00:20:26.747
No.

369
00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.162
I should check on the new
arrivals in the apartment.

370
00:20:31.186 --> 00:20:32.706
Hopefully I can get
some answers there.

371
00:20:42.719 --> 00:20:44.373
Hey. you okay?

372
00:21:01.521 --> 00:21:02.913
-Leonard!
-Yeah?

373
00:21:03.566 --> 00:21:04.654
We're going on lockdown.

374
00:21:04.785 --> 00:21:06.482
I want guards in the pantry
and the armory.

375
00:21:06.569 --> 00:21:08.571
With everything happening.
we can't be too careful.

376
00:21:08.702 --> 00:21:09.746
You got it.

377
00:21:09.833 --> 00:21:10.660
Hey. guys!
We're going on lockdown!

378
00:21:10.791 --> 00:21:12.009
Where the hell is Negan?

379
00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.820
I'm gonna need you in
the armory.

380
00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.366
Shoulda faced
the truth and just moved on.

381
00:21:20.453 --> 00:21:21.454
Moved on how?

382
00:21:21.541 --> 00:21:22.779
After you destroyed
everything we had?

383
00:21:25.632 --> 00:21:27.111
Two groups of people.

384
00:21:28.112 --> 00:21:29.940
But only one can stay.

385
00:21:30.941 --> 00:21:33.074
However will we decide?

386
00:21:37.383 --> 00:21:40.124
See. I used to know this...

387
00:21:40.255 --> 00:21:42.779
Well. we'll call him an asshole.

388
00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.087
And he would ask people
three questions.

389
00:21:46.174 --> 00:21:47.654
and that would decide
whether or not

390
00:21:47.784 --> 00:21:50.134
they would stay as part
of the community.

391
00:21:50.831 --> 00:21:54.661
But see. I am not in the mood
to be asking any questions.

392
00:21:56.097 --> 00:21:57.794
So we're gonna play a game.

393
00:21:59.056 --> 00:22:02.016
We are gonna play Piñata.

394
00:22:02.146 --> 00:22:06.020
And you two are stuffed full of

395
00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.457
poo-poo-flavored candy.

396
00:22:09.632 --> 00:22:10.851
Dillard!

397
00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.984
See. Dillard. occasionally

398
00:22:14.115 --> 00:22:16.378
you have to crack a couple eggs.

399
00:22:16.465 --> 00:22:17.785
Otherwise. you're left
cleaning up

400
00:22:17.814 --> 00:22:20.426
a big-ol' eggy mess.

401
00:22:24.255 --> 00:22:29.130
I am tired of
the he said/she said bullshit.

402
00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:32.829
So we're gonna let Dizzy Dillard
here take some swings

403
00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:34.309
until one of you volunteer

404
00:22:34.396 --> 00:22:36.964
to take your people out
of Manhattan.

405
00:22:38.008 --> 00:22:39.662
Dillard?

406
00:22:41.795 --> 00:22:43.840
♪ Dale. dale. dale! ♪

407
00:22:43.927 --> 00:22:46.234
♪ You can't miss 'em.
Dillard ♪

408
00:22:48.671 --> 00:22:52.632
♪ One of you is leaving.
or both of you are dead ♪

409
00:22:54.329 --> 00:22:59.465
♪ Dale. dale. dale.
bashing in some heads ♪

410
00:22:59.595 --> 00:23:01.075
Oh! Shh...

411
00:23:02.946 --> 00:23:06.428
Oh! Oopsie-daisy.

412
00:23:08.082 --> 00:23:10.432
Somebody forgot
to pay the power bill!

413
00:23:10.519 --> 00:23:12.869
You know how we make
electricity?

414
00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.523
Bodies.

415
00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:17.004
That's right.
We live off the dead.

416
00:23:17.091 --> 00:23:20.094
So unless one of you pipes up.

417
00:23:20.224 --> 00:23:23.663
we will gladly kill
all of your people.

418
00:23:27.318 --> 00:23:28.755
Seriously?

419
00:23:29.886 --> 00:23:32.628
You would rather have your kids

420
00:23:32.715 --> 00:23:35.762
power up my Xbox...

421
00:23:37.241 --> 00:23:40.375
than squash this little
beef you have?

422
00:23:48.514 --> 00:23:50.777
Alright. Got that.

423
00:23:57.087 --> 00:23:58.306
Hey.

424
00:23:59.786 --> 00:24:01.527
Hey. I'm comin'.

425
00:24:04.878 --> 00:24:06.140
Oh. yeah. I feel this one.

426
00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:18.326
Did you?

427
00:24:18.413 --> 00:24:19.762
Oh. come on.

428
00:24:19.849 --> 00:24:21.889
We just had a little bit of
a heart-to-heart is all.

429
00:24:22.286 --> 00:24:24.071
Look. I don't know
who started it.

430
00:24:24.158 --> 00:24:26.987
but neither asshole is innocent.

431
00:24:27.074 --> 00:24:28.510
The war is not gonna end.

432
00:24:28.641 --> 00:24:30.207
which means all we got
to do is...

433
00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:33.646
Wow. Still?

434
00:24:33.733 --> 00:24:35.517
-For reals with this?
-Christ.

435
00:24:35.648 --> 00:24:37.388
How many guards does it take
to load a tank?

436
00:24:37.476 --> 00:24:38.346
More.

437
00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:43.360
What the hell
are they doing down there?

438
00:24:44.221 --> 00:24:46.572
You are so gonna owe us.

439
00:24:48.661 --> 00:24:52.534
No! No. wake up!

440
00:24:52.621 --> 00:24:55.798
Please. stay!

441
00:24:59.802 --> 00:25:01.587
Hershel. no!

442
00:25:05.852 --> 00:25:07.201
I have to try.

443
00:25:40.713 --> 00:25:42.279
All four ventilators
just went down.

444
00:25:42.366 --> 00:25:43.779
If we don't Ambu bag. they're
brain dead in five minutes.

445
00:25:43.803 --> 00:25:46.327
Here. bag Damien.
Can you do bed six?

446
00:25:46.414 --> 00:25:48.111
-Yep.
-Ever done this before?

447
00:25:48.198 --> 00:25:49.198
Once.

448
00:25:49.243 --> 00:25:50.636
Connect it to
the breathing tube.

449
00:25:50.723 --> 00:25:52.563
-Squeeze every six seconds.
-Every six seconds.

450
00:26:22.972 --> 00:26:24.278
Mom. duck!

451
00:26:29.413 --> 00:26:30.676
Bone saw. wall cabinet.

452
00:26:40.424 --> 00:26:41.817
Here.

453
00:26:41.904 --> 00:26:43.384
Please. Please.

454
00:26:43.471 --> 00:26:45.691
Do you have anything
to give me for the pain?

455
00:26:48.084 --> 00:26:49.738
It's the best I've got.

456
00:27:07.626 --> 00:27:09.323
By the time I get down here...

457
00:27:11.238 --> 00:27:12.631
They turned.

458
00:27:12.761 --> 00:27:14.001
Must have got bit by a patient.

459
00:27:16.417 --> 00:27:19.463
Alright. come on.
Dillweed. let's keep movin'.

460
00:27:26.122 --> 00:27:27.471
Dillard.

461
00:27:31.127 --> 00:27:32.651
Oh!

462
00:27:33.782 --> 00:27:36.002
Aah! Get off me!

463
00:27:36.132 --> 00:27:38.004
Aah!

464
00:27:39.527 --> 00:27:41.921
-Help me! Help me!
-Stay under there!

465
00:28:11.951 --> 00:28:13.169
Hey. man.

466
00:28:13.909 --> 00:28:17.217
Oh. shit!

467
00:28:22.831 --> 00:28:24.703
We should've stayed at the bar.

468
00:28:26.748 --> 00:28:28.588
It's good to get out on the town
with you. man.

469
00:28:32.362 --> 00:28:33.712
We need to bag bed three soon.

470
00:28:33.842 --> 00:28:35.844
Hey. I know you're at war
with these two.

471
00:28:35.931 --> 00:28:38.847
If they die. we all die.
Can't you help?

472
00:28:49.031 --> 00:28:50.119
-Luis?!
-I got it!

473
00:28:50.206 --> 00:28:51.773
Keep bagging!

474
00:29:11.575 --> 00:29:13.229
Help me!

475
00:29:13.316 --> 00:29:16.015
Help me! Help me!

476
00:29:18.582 --> 00:29:19.845
Help me!

477
00:29:25.894 --> 00:29:29.071
-Hershel. did you hear that?
-Hear what?

478
00:29:32.553 --> 00:29:33.859
One.

479
00:29:35.556 --> 00:29:36.949
Two.

480
00:29:39.429 --> 00:29:40.561
Three.

481
00:29:45.958 --> 00:29:47.263
Four.

482
00:29:49.265 --> 00:29:50.745
Five.

483
00:29:52.051 --> 00:29:53.139
Six.

484
00:30:42.188 --> 00:30:44.190
Hey.
What's up. Doc?

485
00:30:48.847 --> 00:30:50.457
How am I supposed to
tell his family

486
00:30:50.544 --> 00:30:52.024
he died from a broken arm?

487
00:30:53.416 --> 00:30:54.591
We do it together.

488
00:30:55.418 --> 00:30:58.073
We tell them it could have been
an embolism from the fracture

489
00:30:58.160 --> 00:30:59.901
or something completely
unrelated.

490
00:30:59.988 --> 00:31:01.642
a heart attack or aneurysm.

491
00:31:01.990 --> 00:31:03.470
Because that's all we know.

492
00:31:04.819 --> 00:31:05.951
Hey.

493
00:31:07.256 --> 00:31:08.388
You lost a patient.

494
00:31:09.389 --> 00:31:10.389
It hurts.

495
00:31:11.086 --> 00:31:12.740
It'll always hurt.

496
00:31:15.134 --> 00:31:16.613
Look at the people you saved.

497
00:31:25.666 --> 00:31:30.801
Listen. I know this medical
school throws you right in.

498
00:31:30.889 --> 00:31:34.370
and the student social life.
well. sucks.

499
00:31:35.154 --> 00:31:36.895
But I will tell you.
you're gonna earn

500
00:31:37.025 --> 00:31:38.940
a pretty kick-ass handwritten

501
00:31:39.027 --> 00:31:41.073
certificate of doctorhood
from me.

502
00:31:42.378 --> 00:31:43.423
Framed.

503
00:31:50.560 --> 00:31:52.998
Bauer and Claudia.
they are locked

504
00:31:53.085 --> 00:31:57.741
into this prick-measuring
contest of epic-ass proportions.

505
00:31:57.828 --> 00:31:59.178
The fact of the matter is.

506
00:31:59.265 --> 00:32:01.310
and I do know
you love your facts.

507
00:32:01.441 --> 00:32:04.661
you can choose a group to stay
and send the other one off.

508
00:32:04.748 --> 00:32:06.881
but it's just a matter
of time before the next attack.

509
00:32:06.968 --> 00:32:10.276
So you let them
finish their little war.

510
00:32:10.929 --> 00:32:14.410
Whichever group survives. stays.

511
00:32:15.107 --> 00:32:16.108
You're right.

512
00:32:17.196 --> 00:32:19.285
This war does have to end.

513
00:32:19.415 --> 00:32:21.809
As long as these groups are
fighting each other.

514
00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:23.376
Manhattan is at risk.

515
00:32:23.463 --> 00:32:26.640
And yes. letting them battle
to the death.

516
00:32:26.727 --> 00:32:28.381
that is a solution.

517
00:32:28.468 --> 00:32:32.254
But it can't be the only one.

518
00:32:33.516 --> 00:32:35.823
We three. we were enemies
when we first met.

519
00:32:35.954 --> 00:32:37.303
Until the baby gave us

520
00:32:37.433 --> 00:32:39.566
something to work for together.

521
00:32:39.653 --> 00:32:41.611
We gotta give 'em something
to fight for.

522
00:32:46.616 --> 00:32:48.314
Revenge is a cage.

523
00:32:48.749 --> 00:32:53.101
The only escape comes from
putting our emotions aside.

524
00:32:56.713 --> 00:32:58.933
These fields are enormous.

525
00:32:59.586 --> 00:33:02.371
It will take each
and every one of your hands

526
00:33:02.458 --> 00:33:03.720
to bring it to life.

527
00:33:04.547 --> 00:33:08.725
Now. you can use these scythes
to turn on each other.

528
00:33:08.812 --> 00:33:12.903
or you could use these scythes

529
00:33:12.991 --> 00:33:15.994
to turn this parkland
into farmland.

530
00:33:17.647 --> 00:33:20.215
Here. survival is not enough.

531
00:33:20.824 --> 00:33:25.699
Here. together. we live.

532
00:34:48.824 --> 00:34:51.741
Well. maybe she does got it.

533
00:35:02.317 --> 00:35:04.363
I don't know what happened
across the river.

534
00:35:04.972 --> 00:35:06.887
But your people are putting
it behind them.

535
00:35:08.584 --> 00:35:09.933
Can you?

536
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.402
Hey.

537
00:35:45.055 --> 00:35:46.840
Hershel was a star today.

538
00:35:48.972 --> 00:35:50.104
You're a good teacher.

539
00:35:51.540 --> 00:35:52.628
Thank you.

540
00:35:53.586 --> 00:35:55.153
There you go. Steady.

541
00:35:56.545 --> 00:35:59.287
-How many more are coming in?
-That's it.

542
00:35:59.418 --> 00:36:01.420
Bauer and Claudia
couldn't move past.

543
00:36:01.507 --> 00:36:05.946
But 146 out of 148 chose hope.

544
00:36:11.081 --> 00:36:12.605
There's good people here.

545
00:36:13.519 --> 00:36:15.347
And we saved a few of
them today.

546
00:36:15.434 --> 00:36:18.045
No. You did.

547
00:36:19.873 --> 00:36:21.527
They're alive because
you lit that light.

548
00:36:22.092 --> 00:36:23.137
You took a chance.

549
00:36:23.833 --> 00:36:25.183
You both did.

550
00:36:27.881 --> 00:36:29.187
You were right to.

551
00:36:31.537 --> 00:36:34.714
I've just been thinking
about Ramon.

552
00:36:36.194 --> 00:36:37.195
Chucho.

553
00:36:38.674 --> 00:36:39.806
Marisol.

554
00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:45.812
The idea of losing someone else
is just...

555
00:36:46.682 --> 00:36:47.770
Hey.

556
00:36:47.857 --> 00:36:49.207
Luisito.

557
00:36:52.384 --> 00:36:53.385
I know.

558
00:36:54.386 --> 00:36:56.083
I know.

559
00:36:56.214 --> 00:36:57.389
It's okay.

560
00:36:59.521 --> 00:37:00.566
Yeah.

561
00:37:02.959 --> 00:37:05.223
Yeah. It's gonna be.

562
00:37:12.099 --> 00:37:14.144
I'm looking forward to
looking forward again.

563
00:37:28.550 --> 00:37:30.509
Seeing you
at the hospital today.

564
00:37:30.596 --> 00:37:33.251
you made me so proud.

565
00:37:34.774 --> 00:37:36.254
You're working so hard.

566
00:37:38.473 --> 00:37:39.473
I like it.

567
00:37:39.518 --> 00:37:41.433
Do you? I can tell.

568
00:37:45.741 --> 00:37:47.439
My daddy was a good man.

569
00:37:50.398 --> 00:37:53.619
And I see so much of
his goodness in you.

570
00:37:56.926 --> 00:38:00.452
This was his
and his father's before him.

571
00:38:00.539 --> 00:38:02.280
And now it belongs to you.

572
00:38:06.936 --> 00:38:08.634
Thank you.

573
00:38:22.691 --> 00:38:25.955
Everything that you did today.
you're the best leader

574
00:38:26.086 --> 00:38:27.166
that this place could have.

575
00:38:27.217 --> 00:38:29.307
Youkept us all safe.

576
00:38:37.576 --> 00:38:39.296
We're building the place
that we dreamed of.

577
00:38:40.230 --> 00:38:42.972
It's... actually happening.

578
00:38:43.364 --> 00:38:46.846
Which just makes it
so much scarier. right?

579
00:38:51.633 --> 00:38:53.679
I've been in so many places
that didn't make it.

580
00:38:55.594 --> 00:38:57.160
And this one is different.

581
00:38:59.467 --> 00:39:00.686
If we can't make it work

582
00:39:00.773 --> 00:39:02.446
with everything
that we've got going for us.

583
00:39:02.470 --> 00:39:04.037
I don't think that we ever will.

584
00:39:04.820 --> 00:39:05.865
I know.

585
00:39:06.779 --> 00:39:09.956
But I also know that
we made it through today.

586
00:39:11.305 --> 00:39:12.959
Yes. we did.

587
00:39:15.396 --> 00:39:17.529
Tomorrow's going to look
so different.

588
00:39:18.834 --> 00:39:20.096
With this many more people.

589
00:39:20.227 --> 00:39:22.055
there's just so much more
to consider.

590
00:39:22.142 --> 00:39:24.884
The hospital is almost out
of meds and methane.

591
00:39:26.581 --> 00:39:28.453
We're gonna have
to schedule power outages.

592
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:30.237
And until we clear more blocks.

593
00:39:30.324 --> 00:39:34.110
set up housing for everyone.
we're gonna need

594
00:39:34.197 --> 00:39:36.548
something solid between us
and the walkers.

595
00:39:37.984 --> 00:39:39.681
That's for tomorrow.

596
00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:43.381
Let's take tonight
to appreciate today.

597
00:39:47.385 --> 00:39:48.705
Can I be honest with you?

598
00:39:49.474 --> 00:39:51.258
I cannot stand champagne.

599
00:39:51.389 --> 00:39:52.825
It tastes like cat piss.
doesn't it?

600
00:39:52.912 --> 00:39:54.087
It really does.

601
00:39:54.392 --> 00:39:56.916
Oh. yes!

602
00:39:58.004 --> 00:39:59.397
Much better.

603
00:40:00.659 --> 00:40:01.747
Salud.

604
00:40:02.182 --> 00:40:03.575
Mmm.

605
00:40:09.972 --> 00:40:11.931
Holy meth lab. Crackman!
What is happening?

606
00:40:12.061 --> 00:40:13.061
Ha ha!

607
00:40:13.106 --> 00:40:15.543
Look. we may have lost
the whiskey.

608
00:40:15.630 --> 00:40:18.633
but we are never gonna run out
of booze.

609
00:40:18.938 --> 00:40:22.028
Just happened one
of those Belleville bastards

610
00:40:22.115 --> 00:40:24.596
is also a bathtub gin wizard.

611
00:40:24.726 --> 00:40:27.337
I like the sound of that.
What is happening in my bar?

612
00:40:27.425 --> 00:40:29.514
-Well. I'm glad you asked.
-Okay.

613
00:40:31.429 --> 00:40:33.648
-Follow me.
-With pleasure. brother.

614
00:40:39.915 --> 00:40:41.395
Now don't get used to it.

615
00:40:41.482 --> 00:40:43.266
I'm just giving
the Xbox the night off.

616
00:40:43.353 --> 00:40:45.007
I did say you were gonna
get laid. right?

617
00:40:45.138 --> 00:40:47.532
And you were on
a bit of a roll today.

618
00:40:48.097 --> 00:40:50.099
So pick a girl.
Any girl.

619
00:40:50.839 --> 00:40:52.275
Or boy. Whatever...

620
00:40:52.362 --> 00:40:54.321
Whatever floats
your freaky boat.

621
00:40:56.715 --> 00:40:59.108
I think I smell... methaney.
actually.

622
00:40:59.195 --> 00:41:00.608
I should probably change
my clothes. bro.

623
00:41:00.632 --> 00:41:02.808
-I'll be right back. Okay.
-Alright.

624
00:41:02.938 --> 00:41:04.287
Okay.

625
00:41:16.474 --> 00:41:18.998
He's turning you against us.

626
00:41:19.085 --> 00:41:20.347
Against me.

627
00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:22.175
Hey. stop it.

628
00:41:22.305 --> 00:41:23.872
That man is no good.

629
00:41:23.959 --> 00:41:25.047
I swear if I ever...

630
00:41:25.178 --> 00:41:26.701
Hey. stop.

631
00:41:26.832 --> 00:41:29.225
I'm sorry.
I get so jealous.

632
00:41:30.879 --> 00:41:32.185
Stay with me tonight.

633
00:41:32.315 --> 00:41:34.404
I said I can't. okay?

634
00:41:34.535 --> 00:41:35.971
-Hey!
-Please.

635
00:41:36.058 --> 00:41:38.496
-I miss you.
-No!

636
00:41:40.628 --> 00:41:44.066
I love you.

637
00:41:51.944 --> 00:41:53.032
Are you the traitor?

638
00:41:53.119 --> 00:41:54.163
Can I help you?

639
00:41:54.294 --> 00:41:55.374
We've come to make a deal.

640
00:41:57.297 --> 00:41:59.342
This woman can get
her hands on anything.

641
00:41:59.429 --> 00:42:01.127
You're sending
our only doctor away?

642
00:42:01.214 --> 00:42:02.868
I need you
to make sure he's safe.

643
00:42:04.913 --> 00:42:07.133
If I live here.
I have to live under your rules?

644
00:42:07.263 --> 00:42:08.983
You follow the same rules
as everyone else.

645
00:42:10.832 --> 00:42:13.226
If this is real.
it could be dangerous.

646
00:42:14.270 --> 00:42:16.621
This is the start of
something better for everyone.

647
00:42:21.713 --> 00:42:23.149
Hi. everyone. I'm Aimee Garcia.

648
00:42:23.236 --> 00:42:25.151
I play Renata on "Dead City"
season three.

649
00:42:25.238 --> 00:42:26.631
Welcome. Muah!

650
00:42:31.940 --> 00:42:33.420
Renata is the leader
of her family.

651
00:42:33.507 --> 00:42:35.422
When her father passed away.

652
00:42:35.509 --> 00:42:37.424
she really had to step up
and take the reins.

653
00:42:37.555 --> 00:42:40.819
And she also becomes
the leader of her community.

654
00:42:40.906 --> 00:42:42.971
Everything The Croat had said
about this place is true.

655
00:42:42.995 --> 00:42:44.997
It is a fortress.

656
00:42:45.127 --> 00:42:49.044
The only thing
that we are missing is someone

657
00:42:49.131 --> 00:42:50.369
who knows
how to keep things safe.

658
00:42:50.393 --> 00:42:52.657
Maggie.

659
00:42:52.744 --> 00:42:53.527
I've always loved that
character. and I always thought.

660
00:42:53.658 --> 00:42:55.181
"Oh. we could be friends."

661
00:42:55.311 --> 00:42:57.444
Now we get to be besties.

662
00:42:57.575 --> 00:43:00.795
Let's take tonight
to appreciate today.

663
00:43:00.882 --> 00:43:01.927
I had said to Seth.

664
00:43:02.057 --> 00:43:03.885
"Please write a BFF for Maggie

665
00:43:03.972 --> 00:43:05.800
because she's just been up
against it.

666
00:43:05.887 --> 00:43:07.767
and it's like she's
been trying to carve her way

667
00:43:07.846 --> 00:43:09.238
through this ocean of enemies

668
00:43:09.325 --> 00:43:12.894
"it has felt like
for a few years."

669
00:43:13.025 --> 00:43:14.113
You haven't had a gal pal.

670
00:43:14.200 --> 00:43:15.767
-Right?
-Yeah.

671
00:43:15.897 --> 00:43:17.856
They both are big-hearted
warriors.

672
00:43:17.943 --> 00:43:20.183
I think there's a complete
mutual respect for each other.

673
00:43:20.293 --> 00:43:24.602
They both have a natural
magnetic leadership quality.

674
00:43:24.732 --> 00:43:27.126
And I think Renata brings out.

675
00:43:27.256 --> 00:43:29.607
hopefully a light in Maggie.
too.

676
00:43:29.694 --> 00:43:31.434
I cannot stand champagne.

677
00:43:31.521 --> 00:43:32.890
It tastes like cat piss.
doesn't it?

678
00:43:32.914 --> 00:43:35.047
It really does.

679
00:43:35.177 --> 00:43:38.877
I just feel like you root
for this friendship.

680
00:43:38.964 --> 00:43:42.924
Building a safe community is
the hardest thing in the world.

681
00:43:43.055 --> 00:43:45.255
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

682
00:43:45.318 --> 00:43:47.581
What Renata brings
to the storyline

683
00:43:47.712 --> 00:43:50.628
is this level
of heart and family and warmth

684
00:43:50.715 --> 00:43:54.501
that has been missing
for our characters for so long.

685
00:43:54.632 --> 00:43:56.677
Renata is charismatic.
she's levelheaded.

686
00:43:56.808 --> 00:43:58.070
She's a total badass.

687
00:43:58.157 --> 00:44:00.550
She actually has this weapon.

688
00:44:00.638 --> 00:44:06.165
which I have personally named
Bonita because it is a bone saw.

689
00:44:06.252 --> 00:44:08.733
This is my first time
with Renata's weapon

690
00:44:08.820 --> 00:44:09.821
and I'm being sensei'd.

691
00:44:09.908 --> 00:44:11.692
Go on.

692
00:44:11.779 --> 00:44:13.278
I thought that name
would be very appropriate.

693
00:44:13.302 --> 00:44:15.783
Bonita means "pretty"
in Spanish.

694
00:44:15.914 --> 00:44:17.785
Lauren gave me a great tip

695
00:44:17.916 --> 00:44:20.353
because she said. "You should
grunt when you kill a walker."

696
00:44:22.355 --> 00:44:24.139
And she says it does
multiple things.

697
00:44:24.226 --> 00:44:27.665
It warns the stunt person
that you're coming

698
00:44:27.752 --> 00:44:30.363
and it also makes
you feel less awkward.

699
00:44:32.234 --> 00:44:34.410
Tips from the pro.

700
00:44:34.497 --> 00:44:37.544
I'm literally putting
my life in Lauren's hands.

701
00:44:37.675 --> 00:44:40.112
Oh. shit!

702
00:44:40.242 --> 00:44:42.375
Wow. The head fell
right towards the camera.

703
00:44:42.462 --> 00:44:44.507
Lauren is amazing.

704
00:44:44.594 --> 00:44:47.380
She is such a fearless leader
in real life.

705
00:44:47.510 --> 00:44:49.774
She's a great quarterback
of this team.

706
00:44:49.904 --> 00:44:51.819
I love her and I hope
to be friends with her

707
00:44:51.950 --> 00:44:52.950
for a very long time.

707
